1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,168
My obituary arrived today, printed neatly in tomorrow's morning newspaper, detailing my sudden and very violent end.

2
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:18,804
I checked the date twice. October twelfth. Today is the eleventh. The ink was still wet against my trembling fingers.

3
00:00:19,104 --> 00:00:25,800
It said I would die at midnight in the alley behind my apartment building, stabbed by a desperate stranger.

4
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:33,660
I decided to cheat destiny. I locked all my doors, pulled down the heavy metal blinds, and refused to leave.

5
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:42,936
Hours bled past in absolute silence. The clock on the wall crept closer to midnight with agonizing slowness.

6
00:00:43,236 --> 00:00:50,268
Then, a frantic knocking echoed from my front door. Someone was screaming for help in the dark corridor.

7
00:00:50,568 --> 00:00:57,768
I grabbed a heavy kitchen knife and flung the door open, ready to fight whatever horror waited outside.

8
00:00:58,068 --> 00:01:05,748
A terrified teenage delivery boy stumbled backward into my hallway, begging me to hide him from an attacker.

9
00:01:06,048 --> 00:01:13,416
In my blind panic, I lunged forward with the blade, not realizing my own terrifying role in the prophecy.

10
00:01:13,716 --> 00:01:22,068
As he fell, I read the headline again and realized the tragic truth. Are we dodging fate, or building it?
